# P18-V01 Pull header decode modes and current-revision gate — 2026-10-17T17:22:37Z

- Repository: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`.
- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`.
- Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1, inspected read-only.
- Code commit: `1db3a1c4 fix(remoting): match Java pull header decode modes`.
- Added an invoked Java fixture and Maven drift check for fast and reflective
  `PullMessageRequestHeader` decoding with missing fields, valid fields, and
  invalid `queueId`, `maxMsgBytes`, and `requestSource` values. The Rust direct
  custom-header decoder now forwards the Java mode. Pull decoding preserves
  nullable/inherited fields, fails malformed numbers in fast mode, and ignores
  individual conversion failures in reflection mode. Pull request-code
  selection reports missing `sysFlag` before issuing an RPC.

